 "source": {
  "revision": "Rev 2.0",
  "pages": 4
 },
 "summary": "A family of NPN bipolar transistors in the four-lead SOT-223 surface-mount package, with the collector on both the centre lead and the wide tab. The three types differ in voltage rating: collector-base 45, 60 and 100 V and collector-emitter 45, 60 and 80 V for BCP54, BCP55 and BCP56. All carry 1.0 A of collector current and dissipate 1.33 W. Each type is sold in two current-gain grades, -10 (63 to 160) and -16 (100 to 250). The PNP counterparts are BCP51, BCP52 and BCP53.",
 "key_figures": [
  [
