  {
   "topic": "Types and gain grades",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "BCP54, BCP55 and BCP56 differ in their voltage ratings and in the bias used for the cut-off test. A suffix -10 or -16 names the gain grade at IC = 150 mA and VCE = 2.0 V: 63 to 160 or 100 to 250. The full part number, grade included, is the code marked on the body."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Gain against current and temperature",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = 2 V the typical gain is near 165 to 175 from 1 mA to about 100 mA at 25 °C and near 230 to 245 at 100 °C, then falls above roughly 100 to 200 mA; both curves meet at about 70 at 1 A (Fig.2)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Saturation",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "Driven at a collector-to-base current ratio of 10, VCE(sat) is a little over 20 mV between about 5 and 30 mA and climbs to about 0.16 to 0.17 V at 1 A, slightly higher at 100 °C (Fig.3)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Base-emitter voltage",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At VCE = 2 V, 1 mA of collector current needs about 0.58 V on the base at 25 °C and about 0.47 V at 100 °C; 1 A needs about 0.86 V and 0.82 V (Fig.5)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Capacitance",
   "page": 3,
   "text": "At 1 MHz, Cib is about 138 pF at 0.1 V reverse bias and about 70 pF at 6 V; Cob falls from about 24 pF at 0.1 V to about 4.3 pF at 20 V (Fig.6)."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Package and assembly",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The SOT-223 body is molded in a UL 94V-0 compound, RoHS compliant and halogen-free. Leads are solder plated and solderable to MIL-STD-750 method 2026. Moisture sensitivity is MSL 1 to J-STD-020, with lead-free reflow peaking at 260 °C."
  }
 ],
